project/vrm-multidriver-player-routing: spoint players render through streaming-gltf (>=1.0.10) ModelPool multi-driver VRM. SUPERSEDES the old "VRM players stay on PlayerManager" rule. Mechanism: streaming-gltf model-pool.js multi-driver = each Entity re-parses its OWN VRM from the Asset.rootBytes (retained for hasVRM assets) via _parseOwnVrm (removeUnnecessaryVertices+combineSkeletons, concurrency-capped _MAX_VRM_PARSE_CONCURRENT=4), so N entities of one avatar each get an independent vrm/scene/humanoid - no single-owner bind-pose freeze (the old _vrmOwner is gone). opts.driveVrm=false makes the pool skip its own vrm.update (and the dist<animationThrottleDistance throttle) so the host drives it. spoint wiring: ModelPoolAdapter.spawnVRM(id,vrmUrl,opts,onReady) spawns the PLAIN un-baked avatar url (player VRMs are NOT progressive-baked - baking risks stripping VRMC_vrm humanoid/spring; plain VRM => meshLodDescs empty => no mesh LOD but multi-driver vrm runs) with driveVrm:false; PlayerManager.createPlayerVRM (given modelPool+playerVrmUrl via pm.setPlayerVrmUrl) branches to it, onReady swaps the placeholder group for the pool entity root as the player mesh and runs _attachVrmFeatures(skipScenePrep=true) = initVRMFeatures + createPlayerAnimator + FP head-bone hide on entity.vrm. spoint app.js:301 owns vrm.update. Player pool root is NON-static (matrixAutoUpdate stays true) so app.js per-frame mesh.position/rotation render. Buffer path retained as fallback. removePlayerMesh routes pool entities to modelPool.remove. Witnessed browser-13/14: local player under entity_N_cleetus.vrm pool root, 53 humanoid bones, head bone, animator, zero errors, no orphan placeholder. Related [[modelpool-integration]].